सम्प सम्प, अस्, m. (probably fr. सम्-पत्),
descending, falling, alighting; (आ), f. lightning;
[cf. शम्पा.]

सम्-पाक, अस्, m. cooking or ripening thoroughly,
maturing; the tree Cassia Fistula [cf. शम्-पाक];
(अस्, आ, अम्), reasoning well, a reasoner, logician;
subtle, cunning, impudent; lustful, lewd; small,
little, low.

सम्-पतित, अस्, आ, अम्, flying or falling together,
coming to pass, happening, fallen or met together;
come to pass.

सम्-पर्क, अस्, m. mixing together, mixture,
commingling, conjunction, union; contact, touch;
bodily contact, sexual union or connection.

सम्प्रचर् सम्-प्र-चर्, cl. 1. P. -चरति,
-चरितुम्, to come forth, advance, begin to move;
to go on, be carried on, take place.

सम्प्रजन् सम्-प्र-जन्, cl. 4. A. -जायते, &c.,
to be produced, spring up, arise, come into existence;
to exist, be; to be born again.

सम्-प्रतापन, अम्, n. the act of heating or
burning; inflicting great pain or torture, afflicting;
N. of one of the twenty-one hells, (Manu

सम्प्रतिभा सम्-प्रति-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति,
&c., to shine out fully, be conspicuous, appear, seem;
to appear clearly, be fully understood.

सम्प्रमोक्ष् सम्-प्र-मोक्ष्, cl. 10. P. A.
-मोक्षयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to make free, clear away;
to clear a way for one's self (A.).

सम्प्रयुध् सम्-प्र-युध्, cl. 4. A. -युध्यते,
&c., to begin to fight together, commence a war;
to fight, make war.

सम्प्ररुच् सम्-प्र-रुच्, cl. 1. A. -रोचते,
&c., to appear very bright or beautiful, appear good;
to please.

सम्-प्रवृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, begun to rain;
(अम्), n. that which has been completely rained, a
whole rain-fall.

सम्-प्लव, अस्, m. submersion, inundation; flood;
surging, surge; splashing or tumbling about in water;
falling into ruins, ruin; subversion.
